      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T09:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e From the bug, it looks like the problem is to check the /proc/keys, which I understand.  But I thought odrefresh doesn\u0027t handle the key?  Or is there other reason that I\u0027m missing?\n \nodsign has to be root because it manipulates the fs-verity keyring. odrefresh  does because of file (DAC) permissions (b/191857035#comment13). That\u0027s probably solvable, but there\u0027s no great reason to solve it right now.\n \n\u003e If we need to use root for now, consider adding \"capabilities\" line.  Hopefully that\u0027ll just work and make it less scary.\n\nOmitting the capabilities line means all capabilities are removed, which is what I want.\n\nRoot isn\u0027t really that scary given the selinux constraints (including on capabilities).",
      "parentUuid": "b8970ac4_0f0b517b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 9,
